# docs/styling-plan.md Slice 2b. THE SILENT FALLBACK is what this
# catches: every font API renders SOMETHING for a family it lacks, so
# `expect_typeface` reads the family the TEXT SYSTEM ended up with and
# the family is VENDORED ("Sora" is preinstalled nowhere). THE FAMILY,
# NEVER THE SCALE: nothing asserts a size (DESIGN.md), which is what
# lets the two Apple ramps — 13pt on mac, 17pt on iOS — share a script.
expect label#0 "typeface"
expect_typeface "Sora"
set_text entry#0 "hi"
click button#0
expect label#1 "clicked hi"
# A text style set on a label OVERRIDES the root font, so a heading is
# exactly the label a root-only lowering leaves in the system face; this
# line keeps the heading's AX contract beside the family read.
expect_ax label#0 "heading/typeface"
